Dear Brent,

=20

During my cross-examination at the trial, you specifically asked me for the=
 court records details of the watches, and of the alleged affair.=20

=20

We identified which watch goes to the respondent and which one goes to me.

=20

You asked me twice on the record during my cross examination if I had an af=
fair and I responded =E2=80=9Cno=E2=80=9D twice, on the record.

=20

I would like answers to the following:

=20
If the judgement is inconsistent with the court records of the submissions =
and cross examinations, what is your duty, what is the duty of the court, an=
d what are my rights?
I would like the court records of the trial as soon as possible in order to=
 start the appeal process. Please can you ask the court to provide the offic=
ial trial records.
=20

I am appealing the judgement and will start the process immediately.=20

=20

I will let you know how I will instruct you as soon as possible. In the mea=
ntime, please do not submit anything without my approval.

=20

With kind wishes,

Nadia

=20

=20

=20

BV20D01752

Fraud Unravels All=20

Veritas Numquam Perit

UK: +44 79 1332 8615

US: +1 424 426 9226

