On 10/04/2024, 7:39=E2=80=AFPM, "Brent Molyneux KC" <BMolyneux@29br.co.uk> wrote:

=20

=20

Hi Nadia=20

I don=E2=80=99t know what the process is for obtaining transcripts of the hearing=
. That might be something that Zoe knows the answer to. Alternatively, it ma=
y be something that the judge=E2=80=99s  clerk can assist with.

=20

I was intending to submit to the court a list of typographical errors, beca=
use that is what the judge has asked me to do. Obviously, I have obligations=
 to the court which I am keen to fulfil.

=20

If you feel strongly that I should not be providing that list of typos, the=
n I think you need to tell the judge=E2=80=99s Clerk, so that the judge can indica=
te what happens next.=20

=20

I had intended to produce an order which faithfully reflects what the judge=
 says in the judgment.

=20

Of course, I would send that to you first but it would not be something in =
relation to which you would have much input because I would be simply conver=
ting the judgement into an order. Again, if you do not want me to do that, I=
 think it best that you tell the judge.

=20

If you wish to appeal, you will need to file a notice of appeal promptly as=
 time starts running from the date of the decision which is effectively rece=
ipt of the judgement. You will need to check the time limits. If I were to b=
e asked to advise you on merits of appeal, et cetera I would need to be inst=
ructed.

=20

Best wishes

=20

Brent=20

